  "entity_raw": {
    "name_raw": "Bat Shape",
    "definition_type_raw": null,
    "source_book_raw": "Blood of the Moon pg. 9",
    "definition_raw": "Source Blood of the Moon pg. 9\nYour powers of transformation have been honed to the point where you can wholly become a bat.\n\nPrerequisites: Cha 13, werebat-kin.\n\nBenefit: You can take the form of a bat whose appearance is static and cannot be changed each time you assume this form. You gain a +10 racial bonus on Disguise checks to appear as a bat. Changing from werebat-kin to bat shape is a standard action. This ability otherwise functions as beast shape II, and your ability scores change accordingly.\n\nIf you wear a bat pelt (see page 31), you may choose to adopt a form resembling the bat whose skin you wear instead of your normal bat form.",
    "links_raw": [
      {
        "anchor_text_raw": "Blood of the Moon pg. 9",
        "href_raw": "http://paizo.com/products/btpy91dq?Pathfinder-Player-Companion-Blood-of-the-Moon",
        "href_resolved": "http://paizo.com/products/btpy91dq?Pathfinder-Player-Companion-Blood-of-the-Moon",
